  "meta": {
    "name": "Base: hand two unused pools to Apxium and revoke every role of the old deployer",
    "description": "22 calls on the Base KasuController (0xb0D7Eb2D5036fB85A231D0E243a5b723BA5D2868), executed by the Kasu multisig 0xC3128d734563E0d034d3ea177129657408C09D35 (holds DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE, the admin of every pool-scoped role and of ROLE_LENDING_POOL_CREATOR). 9 grantRole calls give the Apxium pool admin Safe 0x7adf999af5E0617257014C94888cf98c4584E5E9 and pool manager Safe 0x39905d92Fc61643546D0940F97E5B5D0C0FB69F2 the roles on Invoice Financing - Accounting Firms (0x54A98e1baeD45854789B0448ED1277997D64FFFE) and Taxation Funding (0xA30D35aa4eBb885c9c7Bb9de766266CD6a221eBe) that the old deployer holds alone, matching the live Base pools. Then 12 revokeLendingPoolRole calls remove every pool role of the old deployer 0x0e7e0a898ddBbE859d08976dE1673c7A9F579483 on those two pools and on Professional Fee Funding - Accounting Firms (0xe621eC2A0De3C9EAb96e088256b60c59FFF87607), and revokeRole removes its ROLE_LENDING_POOL_CREATOR. Grants come first so no pool is ever left without an admin. Idempotent.",
    "txBuilderVersion": "1.16.5",
    "createdFromSafeAddress": "0xC3128d734563E0d034d3ea177129657408C09D35",
    "createdFromOwnerAddress": "",
    "checksum": ""
